## 2026-08-19 — Task: "Other Income" text below graph is cut off (re-opened)

- The human re-opened this after c400999's offset/height tweak. Measured the
  actual geometry with a DOM probe (dist/measure.html: a copy of the built
  index.html plus a script that reports getBBox/getBoundingClientRect, dumped
  with `chrome --headless --dump-dom --virtual-time-budget=8000`; far more
  reliable than eyeballing screenshots, and it works around the mount-
  animation gotcha that leaves series invisible in headless shots).
- Result: c400999 did not actually fix it, it just made it marginal. The SVG
  <text> label's bbox bottom sat at y=238.0 inside a 240px-tall SVG — 2px of
  clearance at every viewport width (375/640/768/1280 all identical, since the
  label's y is derived from axis geometry, not from the font). SVGs clip at
  their viewport, so any font whose descender is deeper than the headless
  fallback's (Inter, listed first in font-family, is NOT installed on this
  box but very likely is on the human's), or a larger browser default font
  size, eats through those 2px and clips "($)" .
- Fix: stop putting the label inside the SVG at all. Dropped the XAxis
  `label`/`height={50}` and render `<p className="chart-axis-label">Other
  Income ($)</p>` as normal HTML below the chart, where block flow can never
  clip it. Centred it over the *plot area* (not the container) with
  `padding-left: 70px` + `text-align: center`: the plot starts at
  margin.left(10) + YAxis width(70) = 80 and ends at svgW - margin.right(10),
  so its centre is svgW/2 + 35, which is exactly where a 70px left pad puts
  centred text. `.chart-container--tax` height 240px -> 220px since the axis
  no longer needs the extra 20px.
- Verified with the probe at 375/640/768/1280: label text centre lands on the
  plot-area centre to the 0.1px (240.5/310.5/374.5/420.0 vs plot centres
  240.5/310.5/374.5/420.0), and the nearest overflow:hidden ancestor's bottom
  is ~1000px below the label — i.e. structurally unclippable now. Cropped
  screenshot at 900px confirms visually.
- Noted but NOT fixed (not this task, and it renders fine): the last x-axis
  tick "150K" has its bbox right edge exactly equal to the SVG width at every
  breakpoint — recharts flushes the final tick against the viewport, so it is
  ~0.5px from clipping. If it ever looks shaved, give the chart a larger
  margin.right.
- The human's uncommitted App.tsx edit (further trimming the mitigation
  bullet copy + dropping the section intro) is STILL in the working tree and
  is STILL deliberately left uncommitted, per the previous iteration. My
  App.tsx hunks are in the chart section and don't overlap it, so I committed
  by checking out HEAD's App.tsx, re-applying only my edit, committing, then
