New `describe('the shape every step shares')`, 5 cases. `landmarks(id)` lists
a step's `.chart-container` / range input / `<details>` / `.next-step` in DOM
order, drops anything nested inside a disclosure, and collapses runs — so step
2 is `['chart','slider','details','next']`, step 3 `['chart','slider',
'details']`, step 1 `['slider','details','next']`. Collapsing runs means adding
a fourth explainer to step 2 will not break it. Two more assert each readout
tracks its own slider. The advanced-inputs describe lost its LTCG assertions
and gained the inverse: the gain slider is *not* in the disclosure, and the
