### What the orphaned change is

The 400% poverty-line cliff of IRC 36B, drawn on step 2's chart beside the IRMAA
cliffs it rhymes with. Read out of the diff rather than written here:

- **`src/utils/tax.ts` (+377).** `FPL_YEAR_PARAMS`, its own table for the same
  reason `IRMAA_YEAR_PARAMS` is — the guidelines come from a January HHS notice
  and the percentages from a summer Rev. Proc., neither of which is the autumn
  one that sets the brackets. `acaMagi` is the page's fourth MAGI and the widest:
  36B(d)(2)(B) adds the *untaxed* part of the benefit back, which undoes the
  torpedo, so this line rises a flat dollar per dollar of other income where
  Medicare's rises by up to $1.85. `otherIncomeAtAcaMagi` is the third solver
  alongside `otherIncomeAtAgi` and `otherIncomeAtIrmaaMagi`, still solved rather
  than rearranged even though its function is a straight line — the charitable
  exclusion puts a flat stretch at the left end, and three solvers that agree in
